## 7. Security & Legal

### 7.1 API Security
- All endpoints require JWT Bearer token (except `/verify/[id]`, registration, OTP, and public landing).
- Exam answer endpoints additionally require the exam session token.
- Rate limits:
  - OTP generation: 3/hour/email, 3/hour/IP
  - Exam session creation: 3/day/user (enforced + logged)
  - Answer submission: 120/minute/session (well above normal; bot detection only)
  - General API: 300 requests/minute/IP

### 7.2 Data Retention Policy
- Active user data: retained while account exists.
- Exam session data (questions, answers): retained for 2 years.
- Certificates: retained indefinitely (public verification requires it).
- OTP records: deleted after 24 hours.
- Deleted accounts: PII purged within 30 days; anonymized exam records retained.
- All retention policies to be reflected in Privacy Policy.

### 7.3 ISO IP Compliance
- AI prompts must instruct GPT-4o to **paraphrase** ISO 27001:2022 clause intent — never to reproduce verbatim clause text.
- Question `clause_ref` field cites the clause/annex for reference (educational attribution), not reproduction.
- Terms of Service disclaims that ISO-Audit360.com is not affiliated with ISO, BSI, or any accreditation body.

### 7.4 Privacy Policy (Required at Launch)
Must cover:
- Data collected (registration fields, IP, device fingerprint, exam responses).
- Purpose of collection (exam delivery, fraud prevention, certificate issuance).
- Data retention periods (per Section 7.2).
- User rights (access, correction, erasure, portability — GDPR Articles 15–20).
- Third-party processors: OpenAI (data processing), Resend (email), Supabase (data storage), Cloudflare R2 (file storage), Fly.io (compute).
- Contact email for DPO/privacy requests.

### 7.5 Terms of Service (Required at Launch)
Must cover:
- Exam integrity rules and consequences of violation.
- Certificate validity and limitations (not an ISO-accredited certification).
- IP disclaimer (ISO 27001:2022 is a trademark of ISO/BSI).
- Limitation of liability.
- Account termination rights.

### 7.6 Fraud Detection
- Log IP address, user agent, and device fingerprint per exam attempt in `exam_sessions`.
- Flag: perfect score (50/50) with average time-per-question < 4 seconds → admin review queue.
- Flag: > 5 exam attempts from the same IP within 24 hours → temporary IP block.
- Admin can manually revoke certificates from the admin panel.

